            <ArticleTitle>[Normal indices of left ventricular function assessed by using computer technology].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>97-100</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>While analysing ventriculograms of 18 persons without any cardiovascular pathology 3 &quot;independent&quot; research workers (to exclude a subjective factor in the appraisal of the left ventricle contours) have developed normal indicators of the total and regional contractility of the left ventricle. The data obtained with the use of angiographic and computer-aided techniques of the recent generation and machine analysis employing unpaired statistics can be recommended for application as normal indicators during the performance of different hemodynamic studies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
